 - *Versions:* a version is a decimal string, a per-user counter (the first version of every user is `1`, strictly increasing; the session rows have a foreign key to their version without a cascade, so sessions are deleted before their version); the newest non-deleted one is the current one (after deleting it the newest remaining one, else `404 M_NOT_FOUND`). `DELETE /version/{version}` deletes the info and all its keys at once and leaves a soft-delete marker (no `auth_data`), so a number is never reused and a repeated DELETE is idempotent (`404` only for a number that never existed). At most 10 backup versions per user: the 11th is `403 M_FORBIDDEN` (never `M_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`, which clients retry; nothing is deleted silently); deleted versions do not count.
